Package: SpaMTPData
Type: Package
Title: Experiment Data Resources for SpaMTP Workflows
Version: 0.99.4
Date: 2026-09-13
Authors@R: c(
    person("Tianyao", "Lu",
           email = "lu.t@wehi.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Andrew", "Causer", role = "aut"),
    person("Quan", "Nguyen", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Provides lightweight, version-aware access to spatial
    metabolomics and multi-omics experiment data used in SpaMTP workflows.
    Resources cover mouse brain, mouse urinary bladder, simulated single-cell
    multi-omics, annotation-refinement, and human brain examples. Large files
    are retrieved through ExperimentHub or verified source-URL caches rather
    than stored in the package repository. A small deterministic synthetic SpatialExperiment
    with a paired transcriptome supports offline examples and interoperability
    tests. Native SpatialExperiment datasets are available in a separate
    resource release; historical archival objects retain their original
    representations. Conversion and analysis are handled by the SpaMTP
    software package. Native experimental files share a Zenodo version family
    with SpaMTPdb without coupling the packages at runtime.
